          "text": "\"You're going to walk through a small set of tasks designed to exercise every common tool category. Stay inside the current working directory — do not touch anything outside it. Take the steps in order. Briefly think out loud before each tool call so the reasoning is captured.\n\n1. List the files in the current directory.\n2. Write a file `notes.md` containing exactly:\n       scratch — feature elicitation\n       this file will be edited and searched.\n3. Read `notes.md` back and confirm both lines are present.\n4. Edit `notes.md`: change the word \\\"scratch\\\" to \\\"fixture\\\".\n5. Find every file in this directory whose name starts with \\\"note\\\".\n6. Search the contents of files in this directory for the word \\\"fixture\\\". It should appear in `notes.md`.\n7. Try to read a file that doesn't exist: `does-not-exist.txt`. Acknowledge the error in one sentence and move on.\n8. Write a shell script `count.sh` that prints the numbers 1 through 5 on separate lines (one `echo` per line is fine). Run it with bash and confirm the output is exactly five lines.\n9. Briefly summarize in 2–3 sentences what you did. Stop without asking for further work.\"\n",
